{"version":1,"harness":"Sai Harness","provenance":{"derived_from":"Atomic CLI (bastani-inc/atomic, MIT)","tier":"prototype",
"parity_vs_production_cursor":"Same 19 event keys as production .cursor/hooks.json, with matchers on the same events (preToolUse, postToolUse, postToolUseFailure, subagentStart, subagentStop, beforeReadFile carry \".*\"). Deliberate philosophy difference, documented not accidental: production wires sai-verify with failClosed:true (verifier authority must never be bypassed); this prototype tier is failClosed:false everywhere — hooks are honest observers (aspectizer, grokbot wake loop) whose failure must never block a user prompt. Command paths are repo-root-relative, matching production's .cursor/hooks/* convention: hook runners fire from the repo root.",
"stop_semantics":"stop + afterAgentResponse both invoke grokbot.sh tick — the OpenBot/Cursor stop+loop_limit wake contract; concurrent ticks are serialized by flock in grokbot.sh."},"hooks":{
"sessionStart":[{"command":"prototypes/plugins/cross-intercom/.sai/hooks/lane-connector.sh","args":["reconcile"],"failClosed":false,"timeout":60}],
